-# locals: caption (AtlasRb::Mash, nil) — the Work's current caption Blob, if it
-# has one, for the link to it.
-#
-# Offered only for a Work with video content: CaptionTrack.applicable? on the
-# edit page, StagedVideoProbe at deposit, where the Blob may still be in flight.
-#
-# The field rides the surrounding metadata form (multipart on both pages) rather
-# than owning a form of its own, because a nested <form> is stripped by the
-# browser and a sibling one would need its own page — the depositor would lose
-# unsaved metadata to reach it.
-#
-# The name is bare `caption`, not `work[caption]`: this is a file the controller
-# stages and hands to a job, not an Atlas metadata field, which is the same
-# reason the Thumbnail input beside it is bare too.
%hr.section-divider.my-3

.my-3.rounded-3
  %h4.pb-2
    %i.fa-solid.fa-closed-captioning.me-2{ 'aria-hidden' => 'true' }
    Captions
  %label.form-label{ for: 'caption' } Captions file
  %input#caption.form-control{ name: 'caption', type: 'file', accept: CaptionTrack::EXTENSION }/
  %p.text-muted.small.mt-2.mb-1
    = "The player shows these captions under the video, labelled #{CaptionTrack::LABEL}."
  - if caption
    %p.text-muted.small.mb-0
      = link_to 'View the current captions file', media_path(caption.noid)
      \— a new upload takes its place, and the file it replaces stays in this
      Work's version history.
  - else
    %p.text-muted.small.mb-0
      WebVTT (.vtt) only — a browser reads no other caption format. Convert an
      .srt file before you upload it.

%hr.section-divider.mt-3.mb-0
